58 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (Participants begin by creating basic rule-based programs in MakeCode, coding the Micro:bit's display, microphone, and sensors to launch simple games like rock, paper, scissors or digital dice. Next, they connect their Micro:bit to micro:bit Create AI via Bluetooth and record accelerometer samples to train a custom machine learning model on specific gestures. They test their model's live predictions to find out edge cases and correct these errors. As the final step they export their trained AI triggers back into MakeCode, binding each motion to a unique mini-game to construct a functional game box.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
59 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 194 0 R
/E (Expected Output. What do participants create, produce or gain from the exploration?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
60 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 197 0 R
/T (Participants collect live sensor data from the accelerometer and use it to train a machine learning model right inside the tool. They make a game box that uses gesture recognition to launch coded mini games like dice or rock, paper, scissors.)
/E (Participants collect live sensor data from the accelerometer and use it to train a machine learning model right inside the tool. They make a game box that uses gesture recognition to launch coded mini games like dice or rock, paper, scissors.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
